	(text "U202A trips above +6.0 V (R220/R221 from +15 V), U202B below -6.0 V (R223/R222 from -15 V): ~12 Vpp sine, either polarity.\nThe wired-OR outputs pull C203 low through D201; C203 then recovers through R224 into Q202's base and through R225, so the LED fades over ~0.3 s.\nR25 (across C203) returns the D201 node to +5 V at idle, so Q202 turns fully off with no dim tail. The LM393 outputs need no pull-up: they only drive D201."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 527.64 111.76 0)
