	(text "U102A trips above +6.0 V (R120/R121 from +15 V), U102B below -6.0 V (R123/R122 from -15 V): ~12 Vpp sine, either polarity.\nThe wired-OR outputs pull C103 low through D101; C103 then recovers through R124 into Q102's base and through R125, so the LED fades over ~0.3 s.\nR25 (across C103) returns the D101 node to +5 V at idle, so Q102 turns fully off with no dim tail. The LM393 outputs need no pull-up: they only drive D101."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
